statement:
Stagewatch can already cue PlayMap playlist items from its running order. A Triggers rule does it: ItemStart (filter n, or label/group/kind), OSC action to <playmap>:9943 with payload "/playmap/playlist/go/<playlist> {ITEM}" (an optional "EXPECT #n" and "AT +ms" can follow), or an HTTP POST of "PLAYLIST GO show #4" to http://<ip>:9940/api/cmd. PlayMap runs it with no token once it trusts Stagewatch's address: TrustedAddresses or OscAllow, or loopback on the same PC.

What is missing is a first-class, receipted integration:
(1) no per-item playout field on RundownItem, so each item takes a hand-written trigger rule;
(2) no standby or item-loaded trigger event, so PLAYLIST CUE cannot go out ahead of GO;
(3) no receipts. The OSC trigger never reads /playmap/reply, and an HTTP refusal (409) only changes the Triggers status line, never Stagewatch's journal or receipt model.
(4) the PatternsLink to PlayMap's 9941 wire sends only the VIDEO whitelist, not PLAYLIST verbs;
(5) PlayMap's trusted list must be set by hand.

The proposed fix (a playout field, CUE on standby, GO … EXPECT through the node's link with receipts) is still worthwhile as a convenience and safety upgrade, not a missing capability.
